---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { SITE } from '../config/site';
---

<BaseLayout title="About" description={`What ${SITE.name} is, and who's behind it.`} lang="en">
  <article class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-12 sm:px-6">
    <h1 class="text-3xl font-extrabold tracking-tight text-slate-900 dark:text-slate-100">About Terminal41</h1>

    <div class="prose mt-6 max-w-none dark:prose-invert">
      <p>
        Terminal41 is a growing collection of practical, no-fluff airport guides — the kind of
        information you actually want before a flight: which terminal you're in, how to get into
        town without overpaying, how long security really takes, where to eat, and what to do if
        your layover runs long. No listicle padding, just the details that make a trip smoother.
      </p>

      <h2>Why this exists</h2>
      <p>
        Airport information online is scattered across dozens of tabs — one site for transport
        prices, another for terminal maps, a forum thread for security wait times from three years
        ago. Terminal41 tries to put the useful parts of all of that in one place, per airport, kept
        as current and specific as possible.
      </p>

      <h2>Who's behind it</h2>
      <p>
        Terminal41 was started by a tourism student with a genuine interest in how airports work
        and how travelers actually move through them — part personal project, part way of applying
        what studying tourism looks like outside a classroom. The site is a work in progress and
        will keep growing with more airports, more detail, and better tools over time.
      </p>

      <h2>Get in touch</h2>
      <p>
        Spotted something outdated, have an airport you'd like to see covered, or just want to say
        hello? Reach out at
        <a href={`mailto:${SITE.contactEmail}`} class="text-brand-700 hover:underline dark:text-brand-300">{SITE.contactEmail}</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
